WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.260
Elon Musk is not a conventional CEO.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.569
And he doesn’t run Tesla in a conventional
way.

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:11.570
In a previous video, I mentioned that Tesla
doesn’t advertise in a world where competitors

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.590
spend billions of dollars on commercials.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:18.140
Tesla also doesn't have a Public Relations
team in North America.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.640
That’s unheard of for a major corporation.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.460
It means Tesla no longer reaches out to or
even responds to the media which is why in

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.830
a lot of articles you read about Tesla, you’ll
see something like this:

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.010
“Tesla didn’t immediately respond to a
request for comment.”

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:37.030
Usually, corporations have a PR team to send
positive news out to the media or to respond

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.370
to their questions.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.500
When things go wrong, leaders depend on their
PR professionals to spin the message to mitigate

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.500
any damage.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.329
But at Tesla, that hasn’t really been the
case since 2019.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:52.440
Keely Sulprizio was the last person to officially
be in charge of global PR and communications

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.440
at Tesla.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.739
She left the automaker in December 2019 to
join Impossible Foods.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:02.000
Nearly every other member of Tesla’s PR
team reportedly left or moved to another position

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.289
within the company.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:05.420
Tesla does have a small communications
presence in Europe

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.210
but not a global public relations department.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.409
The big question is: why?

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:15.210
CEO Elon Musk has had some pretty harsh things
to say about the press.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.040
He believes they treat Tesla unfairly and
once tweeted:

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:22.670
The holier-than-thou hypocrisy of big media
companies who lay claim to the truth, but

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.130
publish only enough to sugarcoat the lie,
is why the public no longer respects them.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:30.939
For example, he called out the media for their
coverage of a Tesla collision in autopilot

00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:33.200
mode that made headlines around the world.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.290
He responded by saying:

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:38.729
It’s super messed up that a Tesla crash
resulting in a broken ankle is front-page

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:39.729
news.

00:01:39.729 --> 00:01:43.729
In his view, what was actually amazing was
that the Model S hit a fire truck at 60 miles

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:46.550
an hour and the driver ONLY broke an ankle.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:51.020
He was also frustrated at media coverage of
the much-hyped Battery Day event in September

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:55.410
2020 where Tesla unveiled it will manufacture
its own tabless batteries to improve range

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:59.900
and power, making a $25,000 car possible in
the future.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.100
Several outlets pointed out there was disappointment
over a lack of an actual battery.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.869
Here’s what Musk said when he appeared on
Kara Swisher’s podcast Sway.

00:02:07.869 --> 00:02:09.959
The press coverage of this event of sad.

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:11.420
Okay, tell me why.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.360
Most of the press takeaway was...

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.360
No battery.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.310
A sad reflection of their understanding, really.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:21.400
However, at the same time, journalists were
reportedly not allowed at the event and weren’t

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.530
able to ask questions.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.780
They had to watch it remotely via Tesla’s
live stream along with everyone else.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.500
The way Musk sees it, there is negative coverage
of Tesla because “journalists are under

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.709
constant pressure to get maximum clicks and
earn advertising dollars”.

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:39.120
He even suggested big oil is behind the negative
coverage since they are “among the world’s

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.370
biggest advertisers”.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:44.290
He’s flirted with the idea of creating a
website where people can rate the credibility

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.319
of journalists and their news outlets which
he thought about calling Pravda - the Russian

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:49.599
word for “truth”.

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:51.160
Nothing came of that.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:55.290
Since dissolving the PR department, Musk serves
as the PR department.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:03:00.200
Much of his communication comes in the form
of tweets to his 58.5 million followers where

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:05.430
he responds to fans, posts news about his
company, and many memes these days, it seems.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.879
He hasn’t embraced ALL social media, deleting
the Facebook pages of both Tesla and SpaceX

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:13.500
a few years ago and calling the social media
platform “lame”.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.739
Musk does do the occasional interview with
the media - he hasn’t completely cut them

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:18.739
off.

00:03:18.739 --> 00:03:21.520
Some argue he really should get a team behind
him.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:25.540
Forbes made a pros and cons list, which, among
other things, pointed out a communications

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.220
wing could “prevent Musk from saying things
that could hurt the brand”.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.180
Besides the pot-smoking on Joe Rogan’s
podcast, or his tweet about considering taking

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.250
Tesla private at $420 a share that got him
into trouble with the SEC, Musk has bragged

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.760
that Tesla cars would be able to drive themselves
anywhere, under any conditions by the end

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.140
of 2021.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:48.130
In fact, he’s said for years that Tesla
is on the verge of Level 5 autonomy in which

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:50.050
no human interaction is needed whatsoever.

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:55.950
However, a public record obtained by the transparency
advocacy group PlainSite earlier this year

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.790
found that wasn’t the case.

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:01.680
This memo from the California Department of
Motor Vehicles notes, “Elon’s tweet does

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.510
not match engineering reality per CJ.”

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:09.970
That’s CJ Moore, director of autopilot software
at Tesla who had a conversation with the department

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.970
in March.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:15.060
The memo went on to explain that “Tesla
indicated that Elon is extrapolating on the

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.459
rates of improvement when speaking about L5
capabilities” but notes at the time of the

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.030
meeting, Tesla was at Level 2.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.680
Musk is known for his optimism, or as others
might suggest, his tendency to exaggerate.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.180
But none of this appears to be hurting sales.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.120
Tesla is selling cars as fast as they make’em.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:37.720
In the second quarter of 2021, it produced
over 206,000 Model 3s and Model Ys and delivered

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.990
nearly as many.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:43.610
The company has said it’s especially encouraged
by the popularity of the Model Y in China

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.590
where Tesla has been expanding rapidly.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.810
And because of that expansion, someone asked
on Twitter whether a PR department may be

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.470
in the cards in the future.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.810
To which Musk responded:

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:57.639
“Other companies spend money on advertising
&amp; manipulating public opinion, Tesla focuses

00:04:57.639 --> 00:04:58.639
on the product.

00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:00.520
I trust the people.”

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.660
Musk will be in the history books for making
electric vehicles cool, fast, and perhaps

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.310
one day, affordable for the masses.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:12.360
Regardless of whether Tesla has a PR department
or not, Musk always finds a way to make the

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.360
news.

